---

<PageLayout
  title="Free T-Shirt Mockups for Etsy Listings"
  description="Free t-shirt mockups for Etsy listings — no watermark, no signup. The Etsy Listing preset exports 2700×2025, above Etsy's 2000px guidance, plus on-model shots and batch colour variants."
  canonical="https://freeteemockup.com/t-shirt-mockups-for-etsy"
  ogImage="/assets/banner/sweatshirt_mock.jpg"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(softwareLd)}></script>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbLd)}></script>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)}></script>
  </Fragment>

  <div class="hero-wrap">
    <nav class="page-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="page-breadcrumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">T-Shirt Mockups for Etsy</span>
    </nav>
    <section class="hero-banner">
      <div class="hb-left">
        <span class="hb-eyebrow">Free · No watermark · No signup</span>
        <h1 class="hb-title">T-Shirt Mockups <span class="hb-grad">for Etsy</span></h1>
        <p class="hb-tag">On Etsy your thumbnail is your storefront. Build a full listing set — flat lay, on model, and every colour variant — at 2700×2025 with the built-in Etsy Listing preset. Free, no signup, and your artwork never leaves your browser.</p>
        <a class="hb-cta" href="/editor">Open the free editor →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hb-right">
        <img src="/assets/banner/sweatshirt_mock.jpg" width="680" height="680" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" alt="Example t-shirt mockup created free with FreeTeeMockup, shown on a white wood background" />
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="page-content-wide">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <h2>Why mockups matter on Etsy</h2>
      <p>Etsy search is a dense grid of thumbnails and shoppers decide in about a second. A design shown on an actual tee stands out where a flat file disappears. Etsy also lets you upload up to ten images per listing, and a full set answers the sizing, colour and fit questions that otherwise send a buyer back to search.</p>

      <h2>Export at the size Etsy actually wants</h2>
      <p>Etsy recommends at least 2000&nbsp;pixels on the shortest side so its zoom works, and crops search thumbnails to roughly 4:3 landscape. The editor has a canvas preset built for exactly that: <strong>Etsy Listing, which exports 2700×2025</strong>. Pick it before you download and the sizing question is settled.</p>
      <p>The other presets are there when you need them — 1:1 gives 1080×1080 for a square thumbnail or an Instagram post, and 9:16 gives 1080×1920 for a Story. Every export is a PNG, watermark-free, cleared for commercial use.</p>

      <h2>Filling all ten image slots</h2>
      <p>Most listings stop at two or three photos. A plan that uses the full set, and what makes each one:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>1 · Thumbnail</strong> — a flat lay on a <a href="/crewneck-mockup-generator">crewneck tee</a>, bright background, design centred. This is the one competing in search.</li>
      <li><strong>2–3 · On model</strong> — two of the ten on-model templates, in different settings, so buyers can see scale on a body.</li>
      <li><strong>4–6 · Colour variants</strong> — the same design on three fabric colours, produced in one batch run.</li>
      <li><strong>7 · A second garment</strong> — a <a href="/hoodie-mockup-generator">hoodie</a>, <a href="/ladies-tee-mockup-generator">ladies tee</a> or <a href="/tank-top-mockup-generator">tank top</a> if you offer them.</li>
      <li><strong>8 · Close-up</strong> — scale the design up and crop in, so the print detail is visible.</li>
      <li><strong>9–10 · Size chart and care info</strong> — not mockups; make these in any image editor. Your print provider publishes the measurements.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For a slot-by-slot walkthrough with thumbnail crop rules, see the full guide to <a href="/blog/etsy-listing-photos-print-on-demand-shirts">creating Etsy listing photos for print-on-demand shirts</a>.</p>

      <h2>On-model shots without a photoshoot</h2>
      <p>Ten on-model photo templates ship with the editor, from studio-neutral interiors to street and beach settings. Your design is displacement-mapped onto the garment, so it follows the fabric's folds and the shoulder line rather than sitting flat on top of the photo. Placeit charges a subscription for its on-model library; these are free and watermark-free, with no account.</p>

      <h2>Every colour variant in one run</h2>
      <p>If you sell a design in five colours across two garments, that is ten listing images. <a href="/bulk-t-shirt-mockup-generator">Batch export</a> renders every combination you select and hands back a single ZIP, named by garment and colour — <code>hoodie-classic-white.png</code> and so on. Your placement is mapped onto each garment's real printable area, so the design lands correctly on a hoodie without you repositioning it.</p>
      <p>It is free, has no daily cap, and runs entirely in your browser. Mockey charges for bulk export; most tools that offer it at all put it behind a subscription. Details in the <a href="/blog/batch-export-t-shirt-mockups">batch export guide</a>.</p>

      <h2>Tips that pair with good mockups</h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Lead with the garment that converts best for your niche, not the one you designed on.</li>
      <li>Keep a consistent background and crop across a product line so your shop reads as coherent in search.</li>
      <li>Refresh a stalled listing's primary image before you touch the tags — it is the fastest test you can run.</li>
      <li>Get the print size right: a standard centre-chest print is 9–12&nbsp;inches wide for adult sizes. See the <a href="/blog/t-shirt-design-placement-size-guide">placement and size guide</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>What size images does Etsy want?</h3>
      <p>Etsy recommends at least 2000px on the shortest side. The built-in Etsy Listing preset exports 2700×2025, which clears that; the 1:1 preset gives 1080×1080 for a square thumbnail.</p>
      <h3>How many photos should an Etsy listing have?</h3>
      <p>Etsy allows up to ten, and a full set gives buyers more reasons to stay on the listing. A workable split is one flat-lay thumbnail, two on-model shots, three or four colour variants, one other garment, and a close-up of the print.</p>
      <h3>Can I make mockups for every colour at once?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Batch export renders every combination of the garments and fabric colours you select and returns them as one ZIP, named by garment and colour. It is free, has no daily cap, and runs in your browser.</p>
      <h3>Do you have on-model mockups for Etsy?</h3>
      <p>Yes — ten on-model photo templates, from studio-neutral to street and beach settings. Your design is displacement-mapped onto the garment so it follows the fabric's folds instead of sitting flat on top.</p>
      <h3>Is it against Etsy's rules to use mockups?</h3>
      <p>No — mockups are widely used and allowed for print-on-demand and made-to-order apparel. Just represent your product accurately.</p>
      <h3>Do these mockups have a watermark?</h3>
      <p>No. Downloads are watermark-free and cleared for commercial use, on every garment and every template, with no signup and no daily limit.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-cta-block">
      <h2>Start making free mockups</h2>
      <p>No signup, no watermark, commercial use — in under a minute.</p>
      <a href="/editor" class="btn-hero-primary">Open the Free Mockup Generator</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
